  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/rachoviscus_crassiceps_en/",
      "html": "<p>Rachoviscus: dedication name for Arthur Rachow. crassiceps: composed from a Latin and an ancient Greek word, means \"with thick head\". Suggested common name: Cherryfin tetra.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/rachoviscus_crassiceps_en/",
      "html": "<p>This beautiful tetra is only very occasionally available, and only a limited number of them are on offer. Origin: bred. Available size: 3-4 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/rachoviscus_crassiceps_en/",
      "html": "<p>In nature, R. crassiceps inhabits brooks with soft and acidic water in the south of Brazil.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/rachoviscus_crassiceps_en/",
      "html": "<p>These are subtropical fish that need no additional heater in indoor aquaria, except in the breeding season. The regular water temperature can lie between 16 and 24°C.</p>",
      "fixed": true
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/rachoviscus_crassiceps_en/",
      "html": "<p>The very peaceful tetras feed on any usual type of fish food.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/rachoviscus_crassiceps_en/",
      "html": "<p>The fish is very peaceful. Each aquarist should have had at least once the opportunity to observe the fantastic dance the male performs during displaying, whether in a harmless fight with another male or during courtship. One of the most attractive features is the deep red adipose fin.</p>"
    }
  ],
